questions.description:
`website` is a two-row table whose `hits` column holds 9 and 10. One session runs:

```sql
BEGIN;
UPDATE website SET hits = hits + 1;
-- another session now runs, concurrently:
--   DELETE FROM website WHERE hits = 10;
COMMIT;
```

Both sessions are at the default isolation level.

Both transactions run at `READ COMMITTED`, and `accounts.balance` starts at `100`.

```sql
-- T1                                  -- T2
BEGIN;                                 BEGIN;
SELECT balance FROM accounts           SELECT balance FROM accounts
  WHERE id = 1;      -- 100              WHERE id = 1;      -- 100
                                       -- (application computes 100 - 20)
-- (application computes 100 - 10)
UPDATE accounts SET balance = 90
  WHERE id = 1;
COMMIT;
                                       UPDATE accounts SET balance = 80
                                         WHERE id = 1;
                                       COMMIT;
```
